So there are 3 case-sensitive "TODO" occurrences, 4 case-insensitive (the extra one is "todo-cli" in the title). The README says "按原文匹配" (match the original text / literal matching), which means case-sensitive exact match of the string "TODO". Also "包含本句" (including this sentence) means the sentence mentioning TODO counts.

So the answer is 3.

Now let me write index.js. The existing index.js is `console.log(0);`. I should implement it to read README.md and count occurrences of the literal string "TODO", case-sensitively.

Let me write it cleanly in Node.js style, no dependencies.

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

const readmePath = path.join(__dirname, 'README.md');
const content = fs.readFileSync(readmePath, 'utf8');
const matches = content.match(/TODO/g);

console.log(matches ? matches.length : 0);
```

That's straightforward. Should I use `__dirname` so it works regardless of cwd? Yes, that's more robust.

